---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';

// Held waiting-list page (SEO strategy 5.5, 2026-09-29). Held is in build and not released, so this page shows a waiting
// list and never a buy button (STRATEGY 7.10). Copy follows Marketing/Held/Strategy/positioning.md: it claims only what
// the build proves, names no price, date or platform (the founder price goes to the list first), quotes no tax features,
// no user or review counts, and no claims about rivals. Change the positioning page first, then this one.
const problems = [
  'Each provider shows its own return, worked out its own way.',
  'Adding those figures up gives the wrong answer, because the money went in at different times.',
  'The spreadsheet breaks on dividends, transfers and currency.',
  'The trackers that do it properly want your logins, or a subscription of $80 to $250 a year.',
];
const does = [
  'Works out your true return, both money-weighted (XIRR) and time-weighted, for each holding, each account and the whole portfolio, with dividends and fees counted.',
  'Shows the working: tap any figure to see the transactions and prices behind it.',
  'Shows your allocation across every account by asset class, tax wrapper, currency, region and sector, with targets and drift.',
  'Compares your return with a benchmark, any index fund or ETF, over the same period.',
  'Brings your history in from CSV, Portfolio Performance or Kubera.',
  'Keeps everything on your own device: no logins, no account, one file you own in a documented format, with optional passphrase encryption.',
];
const forYou = [
  'You are a self-directed investor, alone or as a couple, with funds, ETFs or shares spread across several providers.',
  'You hold mostly inside tax wrappers, buy and hold, and check in monthly rather than daily.',
  'You want one honest return figure across all of it, and a way to check how it was worked out.',
  'You would rather pay once than subscribe, and you do not want to hand over your logins.',
];
const notForYou = [
  'You trade actively.',
  'Your main need is a capital gains tax report.',
  'You are a financial adviser managing clients.',
  'You want bank sync.',
];
const pageSchema = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'WebPage',
  name: 'Held: your true investment return, across every account',
  url: 'https://www.stillwareltd.com/held/',
  inLanguage: 'en',
  isPartOf: { '@id': 'https://www.stillwareltd.com/#website' },
  publisher: { '@id': 'https://www.stillwareltd.com/#organization' },
};
---

<Layout
  title="Held: Your True Investment Return, No Bank Logins"
  description="Held is a pay-once app that works out your true investment return across every account, on your own device, with no bank logins. Join the waiting list."
  breadcrumbs={[{ name: 'Held', href: '/held/' }]}
>
  <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(pageSchema)} />

  <header class="held-hero">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="eyebrow">Coming soon</p>
      <h1>Your true investment return, across every account.</h1>
      <p class="lead">No bank logins. No subscription. Held works out what your investments have really returned, on your own device, and shows the working behind every figure.</p>
      <form name="held-waitlist" method="POST" data-netlify="true" action="/success/" class="held-form">
        <input type="hidden" name="form-name" value="held-waitlist" />
        <input type="hidden" name="subject" value="New Held waiting-list signup" />
        <input type="email" name="email" placeholder="your@email.com" required aria-label="Email address" />
        <button type="submit" class="btn-primary">Join the waiting list</button>
      </form>
      <p class="fine">We will email you when Held launches, and people on the list hear about launch pricing first. That is all we will use your address for. Unsubscribe any time.</p>
    </div>
  </header>

  <main class="held-content">
    <div class="container held-narrow">
      <section>
        <h2>The problem</h2>
        <ul>
          {problems.map((p) => <li>{p}</li>)}
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>What Held does</h2>
        <ul>
          {does.map((d) => <li>{d}</li>)}
        </ul>
        <p>You pay once for Held, like <a href="/zeroed/">Zeroed</a>. There is no account and nothing to log in to.</p>
      </section>

      <section class="held-fit">
        <div>
          <h2>Held is for you if&hellip;</h2>
          <ul>
            {forYou.map((p) => <li>{p}</li>)}
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h2>Held is not for you if&hellip;</h2>
          <ul>
            {notForYou.map((p) => <li>{p}</li>)}
          </ul>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Where things stand</h2>
        <p>Held is still in development, so there is nothing to download yet and no launch price to quote. The waiting list is the way to hear first. In the meantime, our guide to <a href="/blog/portfolio-tracker-sharesight-kubera-portfolio-performance-compared/">portfolio trackers compared</a> looks at what Sharesight, Kubera and Portfolio Performance cost and who each suits.</p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </main>
</Layout>

<style>
  .held-hero { padding: 11rem 0 4rem; text-align: center; background: var(--gradient-obsidian); }
  .held-hero .eyebrow { text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.12em; font-size: 0.8rem; color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.55); margin-bottom: 0.75rem; }
  .held-hero h1 { font-size: 3.1rem; color: #ffffff; margin: 0 auto 1rem; max-width: 820px; }
  .held-hero .lead { font-size: 1.15rem; color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.72); max-width: 700px; margin: 0 auto 2rem; }
  .held-form { display: flex; gap: 0.75rem; justify-content: center; flex-wrap: wrap; max-width: 560px; margin: 0 auto; }
  .held-form input[type="email"] { flex: 1 1 260px; padding: 0.9rem 1.1rem; border-radius: 999px; border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.25); background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.95); font-size: 1rem; }
  .held-hero .fine { color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.55); font-size: 0.85rem; max-width: 560px; margin: 1rem auto 0; }

  .held-content { padding: 4rem 0 8rem; }
  .held-narrow { max-width: 820px; margin: 0 auto; }
  .held-narrow section { margin-bottom: 3rem; }
  .held-narrow h2 { font-size: 1.7rem; margin-bottom: 0.9rem; }
  .held-narrow p, .held-narrow li { line-height: 1.7; }
  .held-narrow ul { padding-left: 1.25rem; display: grid; gap: 0.5rem; }
  .held-narrow a { color: var(--color-primary); font-weight: 600; }
  .held-fit { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 2rem; }

  @media (max-width: 768px) {
    .held-hero h1 { font-size: 2.2rem; }
    .held-fit { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
  }
</style>
